{"id":"mahabharata-7-074","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":74,"title":"चतुःसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 74 · Arjuna makes water for the horses","summary":{"en":"In the afternoon Arjuna and Krishna press on, and the weary horses need rest. Arjuna pierces the earth with an arrow to make a pool, builds a shelter of arrows, and Krishna unyokes and tends the horses.","kn":"ಮಧ್ಯಾಹ್ನ ಅರ್ಜುನ, ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಮುನ್ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾರೆ; ದಣಿದ ಕುದುರೆಗಳಿಗೆ ವಿಶ್ರಾಂತಿ ಬೇಕು. ಅರ್ಜುನ ಬಾಣದಿಂದ ನೆಲ ಭೇದಿಸಿ ಸರೋವರ ಮಾಡಿ ಬಾಣದ ಮನೆ ಕಟ್ಟುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಕೃಷ್ಣ ಕುದುರೆಗಳನ್ನು ಬಿಚ್ಚಿ ಆರೈಕೆ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अपराह्न में अर्जुन और कृष्ण आगे बढ़ते हैं और थके घोड़ों को विश्राम चाहिए। अर्जुन बाण से भूमि भेदकर सरोवर बनाते हैं, बाणों का मण्डप रचते हैं, और कृष्ण घोड़े खोलकर उनकी सेवा करते हैं।","te":"మధ్యాహ్నం అర్జునుడు, కృష్ణుడు ముందుకు సాగుతారు; అలసిన గుర్రాలకు విశ్రాంతి కావాలి. అర్జునుడు బాణంతో నేల ఛేదించి సరస్సు చేసి బాణాల ఇల్లు కడతాడు; కృష్ణుడు గుర్రాలను విప్పి సేవ చేస్తాడు.","ta":"பிற்பகலில் அர்ஜுனனும் கண்ணனும் முன்னேற, களைத்த குதிரைகளுக்கு ஓய்வு தேவைப்படுகிறது. அர்ஜுனன் அம்பால் நிலத்தைப் பிளந்து குளம் உண்டாக்கி அம்புக் கூடாரம் அமைக்க, கண்ணன் குதிரைகளை அவிழ்த்துப் பேணுகிறார்.","ml":"ഉച്ചയ്ക്കുശേഷം അർജുനനും കൃഷ്ണനും മുന്നോട്ടു നീങ്ങുന്നു; ക്ഷീണിച്ച കുതിരകൾക്ക് വിശ്രമം വേണം. അർജുനൻ അമ്പുകൊണ്ട് ഭൂമി തുളച്ച് ഒരു കുളമുണ്ടാക്കുന്നു, അമ്പുകൾകൊണ്ട് ഒരു ആവരണം തീർക്കുന്നു; കൃഷ്ണൻ കുതിരകളെ അഴിച്ച് പരിചരിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.74; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"परिवर्तमाने त्वादित्ये तत्र सूर्यस्य रश्मिभिः ।\nरजसा कीर्यमाणाश्च मन्दीभूताश्च सैनिकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the sun turned westward, the soldiers, strewn with dust and in the rays of the sun, grew sluggish."}},{"n":2,"text":"तिष्ठतां युध्यमानानां पुनरावर्ततामपि ।\nभज्यतां जयतां चैव जगाम तदहः शनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As men stood and fought, turned back, broke and won, that day slowly passed."}},{"n":3,"text":"तथा तेषु विषक्तेषु सैन्येषु जयगृद्धिषु ।\nअर्जुनो वासुदेवश्च सैन्धवायैव जग्मतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"While those armies were thus locked together, greedy for victory, Arjuna and Vasudeva went on toward the Saindhava."}},{"n":4,"text":"रथमार्गप्रमाणं तु कौन्तेयो निशितैः शरैः ।\nचकार तत्र पन्थानं ययौ येन जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kunti's son, with sharp arrows, made a road as wide as a chariot's track, along which Janardana drove."}},{"n":5,"text":"यत्र यत्र रथो याति पाण्डवस्य महात्मनः ।\nतत्र तत्रैव दीर्यन्ते सेनास्तव विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wherever the great-souled Pandava's chariot went, there your armies were torn apart, O lord of men."}},{"n":6,"text":"रथशिक्षां तु दाशार्हो दर्शयामास वीर्यवान् ।\nउत्तमाधममध्यानि मण्डलानि विदर्शयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The mighty Dasharha showed his skill in driving, displaying the best, the worst and the middle turns."}},{"n":7,"text":"ते तु नामाङ्किताः पीताः कालज्वलनसंनिभाः ।\nस्नायुनद्धाः सुपर्वाणः पृथवो दीर्घगामिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those arrows, marked with his name, yellow, like Time's own flame, bound with sinew, well-jointed, broad, long-flying,"}},{"n":8,"text":"वैणवायस्मयशराः स्वायता विविधाननाः ।\nरुधिरं पतगैः सार्धं प्राणिनां पपुराहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"with shafts of bamboo and iron, well-drawn, with many kinds of heads, drank the blood of living beings in battle, together with the feathers."}},{"n":9,"text":"रथस्थितः क्रोशमात्रे यानस्यत्यर्जुनः शरान् ।\nरथे क्रोशमतिक्रान्ते तस्य ते घ्नन्ति शात्रवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Standing in his chariot, Arjuna shot arrows a krosha ahead; when the chariot had passed a krosha, those arrows were killing his enemies."}},{"n":10,"text":"तार्क्ष्यमारुतरंहोभिर्वाजिभिः साधुवाहिभिः ।\nतथागच्छद्धृषीकेशः कृत्स्नं विस्मापयञ्जगत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With horses that went like Garuda and the wind, well-yoked, Hrishikesha went thus, astonishing the whole world."}},{"n":11,"text":"न तथा गच्छति रथस्तपनस्य विशां पते ।\nनेन्द्रस्य न च रुद्रस्य नापि वैश्रवणस्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"No chariot, O lord of men, goes so, not that of the sun, not Indra's, not Rudra's, not Vaishravana's."}},{"n":12,"text":"नान्यस्य समरे राजन्गतपूर्वस्तथा रथः ।\nयथा ययावर्जुनस्य मनोभिप्रायशीघ्रगः ॥","meaning":{"en":"No other chariot in battle, O king, has ever gone as Arjuna's went, moving as swiftly as his mind's wish."}},{"n":13,"text":"प्रविश्य तु रणे राजन्केशवः परवीरहा ।\nसेनामध्ये हयांस्तूर्णं चोदयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering the battle, O king, Keshava, slayer of enemy heroes, quickly urged the horses on into the midst of the army, O Bharata."}},{"n":14,"text":"ततस्तस्य रथौघस्य मध्यं प्राप्य हयोत्तमाः ।\nकृच्छ्रेण रथमूहुस्तं क्षुत्पिपासाश्रमान्विताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, reaching the middle of that crowd of chariots, the best horses, tired and thirsty and hungry, bore the chariot with difficulty."}},{"n":15,"text":"क्षताश्च बहुभिः शस्त्रैर्युद्धशौण्डैरनेकशः ।\nमण्डलानि विचित्राणि विचेरुस्ते मुहुर्मुहुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wounded many times by many weapons of battle-proud men, they still moved again and again in varied circles."}},{"n":16,"text":"हतानां वाजिनागानां रथानां च नरैः सह ।\nउपरिष्टादतिक्रान्ताः शैलाभानां सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"They passed over thousands of mountain-like heaps of slain horses, elephants and chariots, with the men."}},{"n":17,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे वीरावावन्त्यौ भ्रातरौ नृप ।\nसहसेनौ समार्छेतां पाण्डवं क्लान्तवाहनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meanwhile, O king, the two brave Avanti brothers, with their troops, met the Pandava whose horses were weary."}},{"n":18,"text":"तावर्जुनं चतुःषष्ट्या सप्तत्या च जनार्दनम् ।\nशराणां च शतेनाश्वानविध्येतां मुदान्वितौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Joyfully, they struck Arjuna with sixty-four arrows, Janardana with seventy, and the horses with a hundred."}},{"n":19,"text":"तावर्जुनो महाराज नवभिर्नतपर्वभिः ।\nआजघान रणे क्रुद्धो मर्मज्ञो मर्मभेदिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna, enraged, O great king, knowing vital spots, struck those two in battle with nine smooth-jointed arrows that break the vital parts."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततस्तौ तु शरौघेण बीभत्सुं सहकेशवम् ।\nआच्छादयेतां संरब्धौ सिंहनादं च नेदतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two, in fury, covered Bibhatsu with Keshava under a flood of arrows and roared a lion-roar."}},{"n":21,"text":"तयोस्तु धनुषी चित्रे भल्लाभ्यां श्वेतवाहनः ।\nचिच्छेद समरे तूर्णं ध्वजौ च कनकोज्ज्वलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The white-horsed Arjuna quickly cut their two bright bows with two broad arrows, and their gold-bright banners."}},{"n":22,"text":"अथान्ये धनुषी राजन्प्रगृह्य समरे तदा ।\nपाण्डवं भृशसंक्रुद्धावर्दयामासतुः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, taking other bows, O king, they in great anger again pressed the Pandava with arrows."}},{"n":23,"text":"तयोस्तु भृशसंक्रुद्धः शराभ्यां पाण्डुनन्दनः ।\nचिच्छेद धनुषी तूर्णं भूय एव धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya, son of Pandu, greatly angered, again quickly cut their two bows with two arrows."}},{"n":24,"text":"तथान्यैर्विशिखैस्तूर्णं हेमपुङ्खैः शिलाशितैः ।\nजघानाश्वान्सपदातांस्तथोभौ पार्ष्णिसारथी ॥","meaning":{"en":"With other gold-feathered arrows sharpened on stone he quickly slew their horses, their footmen, and both rear charioteers."}},{"n":25,"text":"ज्येष्ठस्य च शिरः कायात्क्षुरप्रेण न्यकृन्तत ।\nस पपात हतः पृथ्व्यां वातरुग्ण इव द्रुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And with a razor-headed arrow he cut the head of the elder from his body; he fell slain to the earth like a tree broken by wind."}},{"n":26,"text":"विन्दं तु निहतं दृष्ट्वा अनुविन्दः प्रतापवान् ।\nहताश्वं रथमुत्सृज्य गदां गृह्य महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Vinda slain, the glorious and mighty Anuvinda left his chariot with its slain horses and took a mace."}},{"n":27,"text":"अभ्यद्रवत संग्रामे भ्रातुर्वधमनुस्मरन् ।\nगदया गदिनां श्रेष्ठो नृत्यन्निव महारथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remembering his brother's death, he rushed at him in the battle, that great chariot-warrior, best of mace-wielders, dancing with his mace as it were."}},{"n":28,"text":"अनुविन्दस्तु गदया ललाटे मधुसूदनम् ।\nस्पृष्ट्वा नाकम्पयत्क्रुद्धो मैनाकमिव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Anuvinda, enraged, struck Madhusudana on the forehead with his mace, but did not shake him, as one does not shake the mountain Mainaka."}},{"n":29,"text":"तस्यार्जुनः शरैः षड्भिर्ग्रीवां पादौ भुजौ शिरः ।\nनिचकर्त स संछिन्नः पपाताद्रिचयो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna cut off his neck, feet, arms and head with six arrows; cut apart, he fell like a heap of rock."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततस्तौ निहतौ दृष्ट्वा तयो राजन्पदानुगाः ।\nअभ्यद्रवन्त संक्रुद्धाः किरन्तः शतशः शरान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing those two slain, their followers, O king, rushed in rage, scattering hundreds of arrows."}},{"n":31,"text":"तानर्जुनः शरैस्तूर्णं निहत्य भरतर्षभ ।\nव्यरोचत यथा वह्निर्दावं दग्ध्वा हिमात्यये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having quickly killed them with arrows, O best of the Bharatas, Arjuna shone like a fire that has burned a forest at the end of winter."}},{"n":32,"text":"तयोः सेनामतिक्रम्य कृच्छ्रान्निर्याद्धनंजयः ।\nविबभौ जलदान्भित्त्वा दिवाकर इवोदितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Passing through their army with difficulty, Dhananjaya shone like the sun risen after breaking through the clouds."}},{"n":33,"text":"तं दृष्ट्वा कुरवस्त्रस्ताः प्रहृष्टाश्चाभवन्पुनः ।\nअभ्यवर्षंस्तदा पार्थं समन्ताद्भरतर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him, the Kurus, though frightened, grew joyful again, O best of the Bharatas, and rained arrows on Partha from every side."}},{"n":34,"text":"श्रान्तं चैनं समालक्ष्य ज्ञात्वा दूरे च सैन्धवम् ।\nसिंहनादेन महता सर्वतः पर्यवारयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him weary and knowing the Saindhava was far off, they surrounded him on all sides with a great lion-roar."}},{"n":35,"text":"तांस्तु दृष्ट्वा सुसंरब्धानुत्स्मयन्पुरुषर्षभः ।\nशनकैरिव दाशार्हमर्जुनो वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing them so furious, the best of men, Arjuna, smiling, spoke softly to the Dasharha, as it were."}},{"n":36,"text":"शरार्दिताश्च ग्लानाश्च हया दूरे च सैन्धवः ।\nकिमिहानन्तरं कार्यं ज्यायिष्ठं तव रोचते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said: The horses are tormented by arrows and weary, and the Saindhava is far. What do you think should be done next, whichever you find best?"}},{"n":37,"text":"ब्रूहि कृष्ण यथातत्त्वं त्वं हि प्राज्ञतमः सदा ।\nभवन्नेत्रा रणे शत्रून्विजेष्यन्तीह पाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Tell me truly, Krishna, for you are always the wisest; with you as leader the Pandavas will conquer their enemies in battle."}},{"n":38,"text":"मम त्वनन्तरं कृत्यं यद्वै तत्संनिबोध मे ।\nहयान्विमुच्य हि सुखं विशल्यान्कुरु माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"But hear what I think should be done next: unyoke the horses, Madhava, and pull the arrows out of them so that they rest comfortably."}},{"n":39,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु पार्थेन केशवः प्रत्युवाच तम् ।\nममाप्येतन्मतं पार्थ यदिदं ते प्रभाषितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by Partha, Keshava answered him: That is my own view too, Partha, what you have said."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":40,"text":"अहमावारयिष्यामि सर्वसैन्यानि केशव ।\nत्वमप्यत्र यथान्यायं कुरु कार्यमनन्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I will hold back all the armies, Keshava; you here, as is fitting, do what is needed next."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"सोऽवतीर्य रथोपस्थादसंभ्रान्तो धनंजयः ।\nगाण्डीवं धनुरादाय तस्थौ गिरिरिवाचलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Unflustered, Dhananjaya got down from the chariot-seat, took up the Gandiva bow, and stood like an unmoving mountain."}},{"n":42,"text":"तमभ्यधावन्क्रोशन्तः क्षत्रिया जयकाङ्क्षिणः ।\nइदं छिद्रमिति ज्ञात्वा धरणीस्थं धनंजयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kshatriyas, desiring victory, rushed at him shouting, thinking: Here is an opening, for Dhananjaya stands on the ground."}},{"n":43,"text":"तमेकं रथवंशेन महता पर्यवारयन् ।\nविकर्षन्तश्च चापानि विसृजन्तश्च सायकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"They surrounded him, alone, with a great mass of chariots, drawing their bows and loosing arrows,"}},{"n":44,"text":"अस्त्राणि च विचित्राणि क्रुद्धास्तत्र व्यदर्शयन् ।\nछादयन्तः शरैः पार्थं मेघा इव दिवाकरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and in their anger showed many kinds of weapons there, covering Partha with arrows as clouds cover the sun."}},{"n":45,"text":"अभ्यद्रवन्त वेगेन क्षत्रियाः क्षत्रियर्षभम् ।\nरथसिंहं रथोदाराः सिंहं मत्ता इव द्विपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kshatriyas, noble in their chariots, rushed with speed at that bull of kshatriyas, the lion of chariots, as rutting elephants rush at a lion."}},{"n":46,"text":"तत्र पार्थस्य भुजयोर्महद्बलमदृश्यत ।\nयत्क्रुद्धो बहुलाः सेनाः सर्वतः समवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was seen the great strength of Partha's arms, in that, angry, he held back many armies on every side."}},{"n":47,"text":"अस्त्रैरस्त्राणि संवार्य द्विषतां सर्वतो विभुः ।\nइषुभिर्बहुभिस्तूर्णं सर्वानेव समावृणोत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Warding off the enemies' weapons on all sides with his weapons, the mighty one quickly covered them all with many arrows."}},{"n":48,"text":"तत्रान्तरिक्षे बाणानां प्रगाढानां विशां पते ।\nसंघर्षेण महार्चिष्मान्पावकः समजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"There in the air, O lord of men, from the friction of the thickly flying arrows, a blazing fire was born."}},{"n":49,"text":"तत्र तत्र महेष्वासैः श्वसद्भिः शोणितोक्षितैः ।\nहयैर्नागैश्च संभिन्नैर्नदद्भिश्चारिकर्शनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Here and there great archers, breathing hard and smeared with blood, horses and elephants torn apart and crying out, the tormentors of foes,"}},{"n":50,"text":"संरब्धैश्चारिभिर्वीरैः प्रार्थयद्भिर्जयं मृधे ।\nएकस्थैर्बहुभिः क्रुद्धैरूष्मेव समजायत ॥","meaning":{"en":"furious enemy heroes seeking victory in the fight, many angry men gathered in one place: so a heat arose."}},{"n":51,"text":"शरोर्मिणं ध्वजावर्तं नागनक्रं दुरत्ययम् ।\nपदातिमत्स्यकलिलं शङ्खदुन्दुभिनिस्वनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was a sea with waves of arrows, whirlpools of banners, elephants as crocodiles, hard to cross, with footmen as a swarm of fish, with conch and drum sounds,"}},{"n":52,"text":"असंख्येयमपारं च रजोऽऽभीलमतीव च ।\nउष्णीषकमठच्छन्नं पताकाफेनमालिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"countless, shoreless, darkened with dust, covered with turbans as tortoises, garlanded with pennants as foam,"}},{"n":53,"text":"रथसागरमक्षोभ्यं मातङ्गाङ्गशिलाचितम् ।\nवेलाभूतस्तदा पार्थः पत्रिभिः समवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"a sea of chariots, unshakable, heaped with the bodies of elephants as rocks; and Partha, like the shore, held it back with his arrows."}},{"n":54,"text":"ततो जनार्दनः संख्ये प्रियं पुरुषसत्तमम् ।\nअसंभ्रान्तो महाबाहुरर्जुनं वाक्यमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Janardana, unflustered, mighty-armed, said to Arjuna, the dear best of men, in the battle:"}},{"n":55,"text":"उदपानमिहाश्वानां नालमस्ति रणेऽर्जुन ।\nपरीप्सन्ते जलं चेमे पेयं न त्ववगाहनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"There is no pond or well here for the horses, Arjuna, in the battle. They want water to drink, not to bathe in."}},{"n":56,"text":"इदमस्तीत्यसंभ्रान्तो ब्रुवन्नस्त्रेण मेदिनीम् ।\nअभिहत्यार्जुनश्चक्रे वाजिपानं सरः शुभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying calmly: Here it is, Arjuna struck the earth with a weapon and made a fair lake to water the horses."}},{"n":57,"text":"शरवंशं शरस्थूणं शराच्छादनमद्भुतम् ।\nशरवेश्माकरोत्पार्थस्त्वष्टेवाद्भुतकर्मकृत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha made a wondrous house of arrows, like Tvashtri doing a wonderful work, with arrows as its beams, arrows as pillars, and a roof of arrows."}},{"n":58,"text":"ततः प्रहस्य गोविन्दः साधु साध्वित्यथाब्रवीत् ।\nशरवेश्मनि पार्थेन कृते तस्मिन्महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Govinda laughed and said: Well done, well done! when Partha had made the house of arrows in that great battle."}}]}]}